\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Stable one-shot gains and their query-prior boundary.} \textbf  {a}, Paired DCTPR gain over BL-NCC for each support rotation. Dots are the ten rotations per episode and orange bars are episode means; rotation dispersion is descriptive because rotations reuse images. All 60 differences are positive. \textbf  {b}, Mean CUB macro balanced accuracy across the balanced protocol and two deterministic imbalance regimes. Uniform-prior DCTPR loses most of its balanced-task advantage, whereas supplying the true class counts recovers much of the loss. Oracle counts are a diagnostic and are never used as a deployable method input.}}{7}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:robustness}{{4}{7}{\textbf {Stable one-shot gains and their query-prior boundary.} \textbf {a}, Paired DCTPR gain over BL-NCC for each support rotation. Dots are the ten rotations per episode and orange bars are episode means; rotation dispersion is descriptive because rotations reuse images. All 60 differences are positive. \textbf {b}, Mean CUB macro balanced accuracy across the balanced protocol and two deterministic imbalance regimes. Uniform-prior DCTPR loses most of its balanced-task advantage, whereas supplying the true class counts recovers much of the loss. Oracle counts are a diagnostic and are never used as a deployable method input}{figure.4}{}}
